  <figure>
    <img src="/assets/images/area-history/1960s/310-1960-ambulance.jpg" alt="Historic image from the Grooving through the Sixties 1960-1969 page">
  </figure>
</div>

<p>In August, the Mandan City Commission voted to support a city ambulance service through a three-party contract with the Bismarck Ambulance Service, which would provide Mandan with an ambulance and driver. Existing ambulance operators Warren Buehler of Buehler Funeral Home and Hector Hoenig of Hoenig Funeral Home had announced earlier that year that they intended to discontinue their services.</p>

<p>During one of the most severe droughts in recent history, local farmers saw crop yields fall by about one-third.</p>

<p>1969</p>

<p>In October 1969, Cass-Clay Creameries of Fargo purchased the Foremost Dairies operation in Mandan. Foremost sold the plant for an undisclosed sum because of its distance from the company's other operations in the Southwest and on the West Coast.</p>
